{{!
Suppresses the deprecation warnings the generated code cannot avoid.

We carry the deprecations from the source specification into the generated API,
so customers are warned when they use them. The generated code must still read,
write and convert those declarations, which warns in turn.

`@diagnose` arrived in Swift 6.4 (SE-0522). Older toolchains skip this block and
keep reporting the warning; the build scripts demote it there.
}}
#if hasAttribute(diagnose)
@diagnose(DeprecatedDeclaration, as: ignored)
#endif
